    "report": "Contact details stay visible after a paid booking is cancelled. The fix is committed on `main` as `f203e97`, not pushed.\n\n**Cause:** The SQL in `hasPaidStay` (`src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts:137`) had a `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'` clause. Once the traveller cancelled the booking, the query found no paid stay, so Messaging masked the host's contact details again. The port's documented contract and ADR 55 both say a cancelled or refunded paid stay keeps lifting the hold, so the clause was wrong. I removed it. Payment status (`paid` or `declared`) alone now decides.\n\n**Test:** I extended the existing e2e test in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts` to cancel the paid booking and check that the host's email is still shown in full. The test fails with the old query and passes with the fix.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The conversation e2e spec passes (15/15).\n- The full Booking and Messaging suites pass (70 suites, 402 tests).\n- `tsc --noEmit` and `eslint` are clean on the changed files.\n\n**Choices and notes:**\n- You asked for a commit on the current branch, so I committed on `main` directly rather than creating a new branch.\n- I did not start a server, so port 4471 was not used.\n- Nothing was unclear in the request. The only judgement call was whether a cancelled booking should still count. The ADR answers that, so I followed it.",
